# Secrets for the STAGING destination (`kamal deploy -d staging`).
#
# DO NOT ENTER RAW CREDENTIALS HERE. This file is committed. Export
# STAGING_DATABASE_PASSWORD in the deploying shell; nothing is stored here.
#
# Read alongside .kamal/secrets-common, which holds the registry token,
# RAILS_MASTER_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY and ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD. The base
# .kamal/secrets file is NOT read when a destination is given.

# One password under two names, and both lines are needed:
#
#   POSTGRES_PASSWORD          read by the postgres image's initdb when the
#                              accessory first boots.
#   STAGING_DATABASE_PASSWORD  read by config/database.yml's staging block.
STAGING_DATABASE_PASSWORD=$STAGING_DATABASE_PASSWORD
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=$STAGING_DATABASE_PASSWORD
